# LaTeX build intermediates. report.pdf IS committed -- it is the attachable artifact,
# and committing it means a reader gets the report without needing MiKTeX. The files below
# are regenerated by build.ps1 on every run and carry no information.
#
# report.tex and references.bib ARE committed: the .tex is the source the numeric audit
# (scripts/check_report_numbers.py) reads, and the .bib is the bibliography database that
# BibTeX needs. Neither is an intermediate.
report.aux
report.log
report.out
report.toc
report.synctex.gz

# BibTeX intermediates. report.bbl is generated from references.bib by IEEEtran.bst on
# every build, so it is not a source either.
report.bbl
report.blg

# biblatex/biber intermediates. The report used biblatex for one day (2026-10-12) before
# moving to IEEE's conference template, which uses plain BibTeX; these are no longer
# produced. Kept listed so a future backend switch cannot commit them by accident.
report.bcf
report.run.xml
report-blx.bib

# The LaTeX templates the report has been typeset on, as supplied by the user:
#   new main.tex            -- the Research Future journal template (2026-10-12)
#   conference_101719.tex   -- IEEE's conference template (2026-10-13), the current one
#
# Deliberately NOT committed. They are third-party documents (placeholder authors and
# guidance text and all), this repository is public, and their redistribution terms were
# never read -- the same caution this project applied to a corpus licence it could not
# authenticate. Nothing in the build reads either file; report.tex is self-contained.
#
# Consequence, stated so nobody is surprised: a fresh clone will NOT have these, so
# AGENTS.md's references to them describe files on the author's disk, not repository
# artifacts. Committing them is the user's call, not an agent's.
new main.tex
conference_101719.tex
